          "date": "2026-10-30 19:19:40.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: drop idle sleeps from insanity 5, 7, 8, 9",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: drop idle sleeps from insanity 5, 7, 8, 9\n\nTests 7, 8 and 9 sleep 60 after failing the clients and again at\nthe end of the test, and test 5 sleeps $TIMEOUT after the OSTs\nare back. Nothing depends on them. In FAILURE_MODE=SOFT, the only\nmode insanity runs in, a failed client is cleanly unmounted, so\nthere is no eviction to wait for, and the HARD mode skips the\nsuite. The later steps wait for what they need themselves, and\ntest 5 already waits for its background clients_up jobs.\n\nThe sleep 5 delays that let a background clients_up start before\nthe next failure are kept.\n\nTest time on a 1 MDS, 1 OSS (3 OSTs), 2 client rocky9 cluster:\n        before   after\ntest 5    64s     44s\ntest 7   256s    133s\ntest 8   276s    155s\ntest 9   257s    137s\n\nThis saves about 380s per insanity run, about 6900 runs per 30\ndays, or about 730 hours of test time.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=insanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I523e6f0d38e4688c5297e8d0e778812c08310705\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
